cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "道德經 · Tao Te Ching — a translation from the classical Chinese"
message: >-
  Citation is welcome but never required. This work is dedicated CC0: you may
  reproduce, adapt, perform, sell, or build on it with no permission and no
  attribution. This file exists so that anyone who *wants* to cite it has a
  stable way to, not to attach a condition.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Ormsby
    given-names: Shalom
    website: "https://shalomormsby.substack.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/opencosmos-ai/taoteching"
license: CC0-1.0
abstract: >-
  A from-the-source English translation of the Tao Te Ching, built chapter by
  chapter from the classical Chinese — never from other people's translations.
  The repository carries the translation, a radical-level glossary of settled
  renderings, a variant apparatus recording where the oldest manuscripts
  disagree, three classical commentaries (王弼 Wáng Bì, 河上公 Héshàng Gōng,
  韓非 Hán Fēi), and dependency-free tools that check every rendering against
  the Chinese it claims to translate.

  Every consequential decision is documented, nothing is asserted without
  evidence, and genuine ambiguities are left open rather than resolved by fiat.
keywords:
  - Tao Te Ching
  - Daodejing
  - Laozi
  - classical Chinese
  - translation
  - textual criticism
  - public domain
  - CC0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# After the first Zenodo release, uncomment and paste the concept DOI here —
# the one that always resolves to the newest version. Zenodo shows it on the
# record page as "Cite all versions".
#
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#     description: The concept DOI, resolving to the latest version.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The translation is the thing worth citing; the repository is where it lives.
# `preferred-citation` gives the book form, so reference managers produce a
# sensible entry rather than a software citation.
preferred-citation:
  type: book
  title: "道德經 · Tao Te Ching — a translation from the classical Chinese"
  authors:
    - family-names: Ormsby
      given-names: Shalom
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/opencosmos-ai/taoteching"
  notes: >-
    A living text. Cite a specific version DOI or commit if the exact reading
    matters — chapters are still being revised.
